tion","verificationNotes":["The supplied name does not exactly match Steam's official name “Rock of Ages 2: Bigger & Boulder™” for App ID 434460.","Confirm the edition or alias using another authoritative source before linking a canonical ID."],"research":{"steam":{"status":"success","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T10:58:45.624Z","error":null}},"steamMetadata":{"appId":"434460","links":{"store":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/434460/","officialWebsite":"http://www.rockofages2.com/","support":"http://forums.aceteam.cl/"},"storageRequirements":{"kind":"required_free_space","windows":{"minimum":{"value":6,"unit":"GB","display":"6 GB","approximateBytes":6000000000,"evidenceText":"Storage: 6 GB"},"recommended":null},"macos":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"linux":{"minimum":null,"recommended":null},"note":"Steam publishes required free space, not the exact installed or download size."},"controllerSupport":{"level":"full","xboxCompatible":null,"xboxEvidence":null,"note":"Generic Steam controller support does not prove Xbox controller compatibility."},"playerModes":{"singlePlayer":true,"multiplayer":true,"coop":true,"onlineCoop":false,"localCoop":true,"lanCoop":false,"sharedOrSplitScreen":true,"pvp":true,"maximumPlayers":null,"maximumPlayersNote":"The public Steam app-details response does not provide a reliable exact player limit.","evidence":["Single-player","Multi-player","PvP","Online PvP","Shared/Split Screen PvP","Co-op","Shared/Split Screen Co-op","Shared/Split Screen"]},"genres":["Action","Indie","Racing","Strategy"],"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":1,"description":"Multi-player"},{"id":49,"description":"PvP"},{"id":36,"description":"Online PvP"},{"id":37,"description":"Shared/Split Screen PvP"},{"id":9,"description":"Co-op"},{"id":39,"description":"Shared/Split Screen Co-op"},{"id":24,"description":"Shared/Split Screen"},{"id":22,"description":"Steam Achievements"},{"id":28,"description":"Full controller support"},{"id":29,"description":"Steam Trading Cards"},{"id":23,"description":"Steam Cloud"},{"id":25,"description":"Steam Leaderboards"},{"id":44,"description":"Remote Play Together"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}]}},"content":{"status":"success","steamAppId":"434460","steamName":"Rock of Ages 2: Bigger & Boulder™","sourceUrl":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/434460/","fetchedAt":"2026-10-16T09:15:38.049375+00:00","locales":{"en":{"status":"source","provider":"steam","shortDescription":"The greatest rock-racing, tower defense, art history game is back! Like the title says, Bigger & Boulder cranks up the surrealism and gameplay with chaotic 4P multiplayer, new time periods, and improved graphics, physics, and destructibility powered by UE4 to be, well… BIGGER AND BOULDER.","detailedDescription":"Featured DLC\n\nAvailable to purchase for $1.99!\nThe pack sees the return of the Smiley boulder and Sisyphus avatar, along with 3 new army banners.\n\n• Owners of the original Rock of Ages get this DLC free!\n\n• Soundtrack included here on Steam only! Find it in: Steam\\SteamApps\\common\\Rock of Ages 2\\Original Soundtrack\n\nAbout the Game\n\nThe greatest “giant rocks rolling through historical/artistic ages” tower defense game is back with Rock of Ages 2: Bigger & Boulder. Just like the title says, Bigger &Boulder cranks up the surrealism and gameplay to be, well… BIGGER AND BOULDER. With an emphasis on the chaotic new multiplayer for up to four rock-rollers, new time periods, and improved graphics, physics, and destructibility powered by Unreal Engine 4, players will need to be ready for some intense rocking and rolling.\nACE Team’s Trademark Quirkiness\n\nThe Monty Python-esque humor is turned up to 11, as players literally rock and roll through the ages. Humorous animated vignettes will also make a return in full force, so famous historical figures beware!\nAn Emphasis On Multiplayer\n\nA little friendly competition never hurt anyone, so that’s why ACE Team decided to improve the multiplayer feature of the game. Play with a friend in local split-screen or up to four players online in a 2v2 match to the death, all with the ability to customize banners and colors for your units and more. Oh, and did we mention that opposing tracks can now intersect each other?\nA Positively Absurd Art Style\n\nJust like in the original game, ACE Team has created various levels inspired by the greatest art periods in history. Players will gaze upon exquisite art from the Egyptians, Late Gothic era, Early Renaissance, and Surrealist movement, as they carve a path of destruction with their rolling rocks of doom!\nHistorically Inaccurate Bosses\n\nTake on works of art come to life in boss battles featuring the likes of The Thinker and the Great Sphinx, leading up to the all-powerful final boss in a showdown like you'd never imagine!\nImproved Physics and Destructible Environments\n\nWith upgraded physics and even more things to be cracked, crushed, flattened, and slammed, rolling various rocks down a hill has never been a more pleasant experience!\nUtter Chaos\n\nWith the addition of brand new defensive units and unique boulders with special traits, chaos reigns supreme so be sure not to take each turn for granite.","aboutGame":"The greatest “giant rocks rolling through historical/artistic ages” tower defense game is back with Rock of Ages 2: Bigger & Boulder. Just like the title says, Bigger &Boulder cranks up the surrealism and gameplay to be, well… BIGGER AND BOULDER. With an emphasis on the chaotic new multiplayer for up to four rock-rollers, new time periods, and improved graphics, physics, and destructibility powered by Unreal Engine 4, players will need to be ready for some intense rocking and rolling.\nACE Team’s Trademark Quirkiness\n\nThe Monty Python-esque humor is turned up to 11, as players literally rock and roll through the ages. Humorous animated vignettes will also make a return in full force, so famous historical figures beware!\nAn Emphasis On Multiplayer\n\nA little friendly competition never hurt anyone, so that’s why ACE Team decided to improve the multiplayer feature of the game. Play with a friend in local split-screen or up to four players online in a 2v2 match to the death, all with the ability to customize banners and colors for your units and more. Oh, and did we mention that opposing tracks can now intersect each other?\nA Positively Absurd Art Style\n\nJust like in the original game, ACE Team has created various levels inspired by the greatest art periods in history. Players will gaze upon exquisite art from the Egyptians, Late Gothic era, Early Renaissance, and Surrealist movement, as they carve a path of destruction with their rolling rocks of doom!\nHistorically Inaccurate Bosses\n\nTake on works of art come to life in boss battles featuring the likes of The Thinker and the Great Sphinx, leading up to the all-powerful final boss in a showdown like you'd never imagine!\nImproved Physics and Destructible Environments\n\nWith upgraded physics and even more things to be cracked, crushed, flattened, and slammed, rolling various rocks down a hill has never been a more pleasant experience!\nUtter Chaos\n\nWith the addition of brand new defensive units and unique boulders with special traits, chaos reigns supreme so be sure not to take each turn for granite."},"vi":{"status":"pending_translation","provider":null,"shortDescription":null,"detailedDescription":null,"aboutGame":null}},"media":{"images":[{"role":"header","url":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/434460/header.jpg?t=1667562890"},{"role":"capsule","url":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/434460/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1667562890"}],"screenshots":[{"id":0,"thumbnailUrl":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/434460/ss_9300a0fd257a4b51f1b2469ed02cf327cf4ccada.600x338.jpg?t=1667562890","url":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/